# Runtime secrets for LOCAL DEV against the Cloudflare Worker runtime
# (`npm run preview`, i.e. `wrangler dev` — NOT plain `astro dev`, which
# doesn't read this file). Copy to .dev.vars (already gitignored) and fill
# in real values.
#
# On the deployed Worker these are set under Cloudflare dashboard ->
# Settings -> Runtime variables and secrets, as Secrets (not plain vars) —
# see wrangler.toml's comments for why that distinction matters (plain vars
# there survive a Workers Builds redeploy; secrets set only in the dashboard
# do NOT, unless declared in wrangler.toml's [vars] block, which is fine for
# non-secret values but wrong for these).

# Resend API key — sends contact/assessment form mail (src/lib/email.ts).
# Without it, submissions are still validated and scored, just logged
# instead of emailed (see sendEmail()'s early-return).
RESEND_API_KEY=

# Cloudflare Turnstile secret key, paired with PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY in
# .env.local. Server-side verification in src/lib/turnstile.ts.
# NOTE the fail-closed policy: if PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY is set (so the
# widget renders) but TURNSTILE_SECRET is NOT, submissions are rejected
# rather than silently skipping verification. Set both or neither locally.
TURNSTILE_SECRET=
